  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 245 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will build from the southern Plains to the\nMississippi Valley early next week, while an upper-level low digs\nover the eastern Pacific off the California coast. A relatively \nweak southwesterly flow aloft will remain in place over our \nforecast area between these features Monday and Tuesday. The low \nlevels remain fairly dry so no measurable precipitation is \nanticipated. A gradual warming trend will occur early next week \nwith highs reaching back into the upper 70s to mid 80s by Tuesday.\nUpper-level ridging will build over west Texas and southeast New\nMexico Wednesday and Thursday. Temperatures will remain above\nnormal with readings in the upper 70s to mid 80s through the\nmiddle to latter part of the week. The next shortwave trough\nlifting from the Desert Southwest toward the southern Plains will\nbring an increasing chance of showers and thunderstorms Thursday\nnight into Friday, especially over western portions of the\nforecast area.",
